    <section class="pg-sec pg-sec--base bg-shades">
        <div class="pg-wrap-3xl">
            <div>
                <h2 class="pg-h2 pg-mb-6">Built for Teams Coordinating Real Operations</h2>
                <p class="pgx-168">Solo sellers can run order management alone. Teams need it. The platform handles role-based access, manual orders, notes, issue flags, and per-order economics edits so your packer, warehouse manager, and bookkeeper aren&#x27;t fighting
                    over the same dashboard.</p>
                <div class="pgx-11">
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="pgx-165">Role-based team access</h3>
                        <p class="pgx-169">Add team members with specific roles, so the right people automatically see the right information.</p>
                        <ul class="pgx-167">
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-145">✓</span><span><strong>Admin:</strong> full access to orders, settings, financial data, and team management.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-145">✓</span><span><strong>Manager:</strong> order management, fulfillment, shipping, with limited financial access.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-145">✓</span><span><strong>Warehouse staff:</strong> assigned orders and fulfillment status; no pricing or deletion.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-145">✓</span><span><strong>Read-only:</strong> view orders and reports, can&#x27;t make changes.</span></li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="pgx-170">Warehouse staff don&#x27;t see margin data. Pickers don&#x27;t need customer email addresses. Everyone sees what matters to their job.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="pgx-165">Manual order creation</h3>
                        <p class="pgx-171">Not every order comes through the API. A customer phones in. A replacement needs to go out. A third-party channel sends an order via email. Create the order manually in Ecom Circles, specify the marketplace, customer, items, and
                            fulfillment method, and it flows into the inbox like any other order.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="pgx-165">Notes, issues, and audit trail</h3>
                        <p class="pgx-169">Orders don&#x27;t always go smoothly. Damaged items, missing components, wrong picks. Flag any order with a typed issue (Wrong Item, Damaged in Transit, Missing from Order, Late Delivery, Customer Request, Fraud Concern, Critical
                            Issue) and the order stays visible in your workflow until it&#x27;s resolved.</p>
                        <p class="pgx-171">Every change is logged: who created the order, who updated it, when fulfillment happened, when it shipped. The full timeline is there when you need to reconstruct what happened.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="pgx-165">Per-order economics</h3>
                        <p class="pgx-171">Cost of goods, marketplace fees, and shipping cost should reflect reality, not your standard estimate. When you bought that item at a different cost, when the marketplace fee surprised you, when shipping cost more than expected,
                            you can edit COGS, fees, and shipping cost directly on the order. Your profit math stays accurate.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="pg-sec bg-shades">
        <div class="pg-wrap-3xl">
            <div>
                <h2 class="pg-h2 pg-mb-6">Buy Shipping and Warehouse Routing</h2>
                <p class="pgx-168">Two operations make or break order throughput: getting the label bought and getting the order to whoever&#x27;s shipping it. Order management handles both inline so you don&#x27;t jump between systems.</p>
                <div class="pgx-172">
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="pgx-165">Buy labels from the order detail page</h3>
                        <p class="pgx-169">Click Buy Label from any FBM or dropship order. Choose your provider and carrier. Print. Tracking syncs back to the order and to the sales channel automatically.</p>
                        <p class="pgx-169"><strong class="pgx-173">Shipping providers we integrate:</strong> Amazon Buy Shipping, Walmart Buy Shipping, Ecom Circles Shipping, EasyPost, Stamps.com.</p>
                        <p class="pgx-171"><strong class="pgx-173">Carriers supported:</strong> UPS, USPS, FedEx, DHL, Amazon Logistics.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="pgx-165">Route orders to your warehouse or 3PL</h3>
                        <p class="pgx-174">If you use a warehouse or 3PL partner, including <a class="pg-link" href="warehouse.php">Ecom Circles&#x27; own fulfillment centers</a>, the order, the inventory, and the tracking all share one source of truth.</p>
                        <ol class="pgx-175">
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-176">1.</span><span>Create a Purchase Order from the order detail page; specify which items need to be picked and packed.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-176">2.</span><span>Warehouse receives the PO through the same software.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-176">3.</span><span>They confirm inventory and process the order in the system.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-176">4.</span><span>They print the label and ship; tracking syncs back automatically.</span></li>
                            <li class="pgx-21"><span class="pgx-176">5.</span><span>You see tracking updates in the unified inbox.</span></li>
                        </ol>
                        <p class="pgx-177">Your team and your warehouse use the same software. No separate emails. No duplicate entry. No lost shipments.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
